From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] usb: typec: tcpci_mt6375: look at the pins again when VBUS returns

With PD off a wall charger took VBUS away for under a second some 20
seconds after it was plugged in, and brought it back. The pins stayed as
they were, so the chip gave no alert for them. TCPM had gone to
SNK_UNATTACHED on the loss of VBUS and stayed there, with the input of the
charger at the USB default until the plug was pulled. At 500 mA that is
less than the tablet uses.

A sink port does not toggle here, so nothing else would make it look. Ask
it to when VBUS comes back while this port is not sourcing it.

On the device TCPM now attaches again as soon as VBUS is back, and the
charger driver follows at its next poll.

---
 drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpci_mt6375.c | 23 ++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpci_mt6375.c b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpci_mt6375.c
index 5cd0bb1923dcf6df84d97a7f84ac7c9589942ef2..42a8b7e16b743ad1203d4d957351c40eea103b0b 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpci_mt6375.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/typec/tcpm/tcpci_mt6375.c
@@ -99,6 +99,7 @@ struct mt6375_tcpc {
 	int irq;
 	bool irq_ready;
 	bool vbus_on;
+	bool vbus_present;
 };
 
 /* What the MediaTek driver clears at probe */
@@ -314,8 +315,28 @@ static int mt6375_tcpc_set_vbus(struct tcpci *tcpci, struct tcpci_data *data,
 static irqreturn_t mt6375_tcpc_irq(int irq, void *dev_id)
 {
 	struct mt6375_tcpc *priv = dev_id;
+	unsigned int power;
+	irqreturn_t ret;
+	bool present;
+
+	ret = tcpci_irq(priv->tcpci);
+
+	/*
+	 * A source can take VBUS away and bring it back with the pins as they
+	 * were. A charger that wants PD and gets no answer does that with a
+	 * hard reset. TCPM takes the loss of VBUS for a detach, and with no
+	 * toggling here and no change on the pins it would wait for good. So
+	 * tell it to look, as at the start.
+	 */
+	if (regmap_read(priv->tcpci_data.regmap, TCPC_POWER_STATUS, &power))
+		return ret;
+
+	present = power & TCPC_POWER_STATUS_VBUS_PRES;
+	if (present && !priv->vbus_present && !priv->vbus_on)
+		mod_delayed_work(system_wq, &priv->cc_work, 0);
+	priv->vbus_present = present;
 
-	return tcpci_irq(priv->tcpci);
+	return ret;
 }
 
 /*
